in 2029 a mysterious global blackout led  to decades of chaos and anarchy the old  nations disappeared  countless micro states emerged  developing their own beliefs and  cultural identity  these are the tribes hey guys pete here  dark is my favorite netflix original of  all time so i got pretty excited when i  saw the trailer for tribes of europa  and noticed the mention that it was from  the producers of dark  that was enough to get me to watch the  first three episodes in an early  screening  and i thought i'd put together a video  about those a mostly spoiler free review  since so many of my subs came to my  channel through my dark videos  because like me you're probably  wondering is this the next dart  the answer to that question is probably  not where dark had this layered story  with multiple timelines that always kept  you trying to put the pieces together  tribes of europa is relatively  straightforward and it's storytelling  so unless what you've really been  missing is the german language and your  tv shows  and oliver masuchi the two shows don't  have that much in common  but that doesn't mean that there isn't  mystery in tribes and while it hasn't  sucked me in in the same way as dark did  i'm interested to see how the final  three episodes of the first season will  play out  what's going on here then tribes takes  place in 2074  in post-apocalyptic europe mystery  number one is what actually happened  back in 2029 that made things the way  they  are there's talk of a mysterious  catastrophe known as black december  because it caused a global blackout but  at least our main characters who were  too young to have first-hand knowledge  of the old world  don't seem to know what actually  happened on that day what followed was a  collapse of the world we know  and 45 years later there's conflict  between the tribes that emerged in the  aftermath we follow a trio of siblings  from the peaceful  originy tribe keanu live and  elia their tribe considers technology to  be the reason the old world crumbled  so they try to live a peaceful life  withdrawn in the forest  living in harmony with nature we meet  three other tribes  in the opening episode the crimson  republic which is  organized like a military outfit they  seem to be trying to put together  something like a civilization  they claim to want to help protect other  tribes but the cost of that  is you basically get absorbed into their  organization  kind of their opposite is the crows who  come off somewhat brutal  they have this urge to expand and even  enslave some of the other tribes but  then they also have this thing that's  almost like a samurai code of honor  where they don't lie  and if they give you their word then  they stand by whatever it is they told  you they would do  the most mysterious tribe is the  atlanteans the arrival of one of their  pilots  who crashes in the original territory  starts things off  somehow they still have advanced  technology and that includes a cube that  the pilot loses  as he crashes and elia gets a hold of  all of the other tribes know about it  and they want to find it first and  that's what brings them to the original  territory he was being followed by a  group of crows  that were being led by one of the more  interesting characters  lord varvara she's looking for the cube  from the wreck  her warriors swoop into the origeny  village  for a pretty violent affair and the  three siblings  get split up the youngest elia who found  the pilot  and the cube originally makes a promise  that he'll return the cube to the  atlanteans  because he was told it contains records  of enormous importance  and it carries a message which is  crucial for the future of humanity  the cuban it's creators of the second  big mystery when he's given the cube the  pilot pairs it with him so he has a  special connection with the artifact  he's told that it will lead him to the  atlanteans base  which is known as the ark while we don't  know much about the technology  otherwise all of the other different  tribes and various characters he  encounters want to get their hands on it  they all know it's valuable  as far as the atlanteans themselves the  character moses  tells elya that it's suspicious that  they still have technology at all  this makes him wonder if they weren't  behind black december themselves  since they must have been prepared for  it considering they didn't suffer the  same setbacks from the blackout that the  rest of the world did  the story breaks down like that keanu  and their father are taken prisoner  and are separated when they arrive at  the crow stronghold  of bratauk which is a sort of fortress  inside what used to be berlin  liv ends up with the crimson republic  after she's rescued by some of their  soldiers  elia is saved by moses who is looking to  get rich by  selling the cube because he's unaware of  what the boy has promised to do with it  we have a peaceful tribe torn apart by  violence in pursuit of some mysterious  technology  liv and keanu are determined to save  their siblings to bring the family back  together  and elia is on a mission that may be  vital to humanity's survival  overall the story is big on ideas which  means how satisfying it turns out to be  will depend a lot on what the answers to  those mysteries are  the vision for the post-apocalyptic  world they inhabit is fairly believable  you can imagine things turning out this  way the budget they were working with  probably wasn't enough to bring it all  to life but their location scouts  definitely did a good job in that  department the crimson republic's  headquarters especially  is an old museum that was built in the  mountains of croatia  the decay of the once futuristic  structure looks right at home in 2074.  most of the look works as i said  sometimes the budget seems a little thin  for some of the things they try to do  there's no glaring weak spots in the  cast  the crimson republic are a little less  interesting while the crows are pretty  cool but maybe a little bit too mad max  the motivations of all the central  characters were easy to follow  and while none of their performances  stand out at this point there weren't  any major problems there either  moses and barbara are the two most  memorable characters  moses and elia's journey is the most  captivating in what i've seen  moses doesn't appear to be affiliated  with any of the other tribes  and his quirkiness adds some humor in  life where elia is a kid  who is essentially a fish out of water  away from his village  since he's originally he doesn't really  know much about the outside world he's  curious about it  so he has this colorful character to  introduce him to things  since there are only six episodes total  in the first installment  i'd imagine we'll see things end on if  not a cliffhanger  than with an open question about what's  really going on with the atlanteans  this could work to its advantage keeping  the story somewhat tight  and then how that plays out could set  the stage for big things to come in the  future if they're able to pull it off  it's a fairly brutal but believable  world there's a pretty graphic  castration  and in general if you like the kind of  post-apocalyptic  dystopic aesthetic there's a good chance  this will be up your alley  and i'll leave it there not the next  dark but maybe something worth checking  out  i think it most resembles the netflix  show the rain  which also imagined that kind of  post-apocalyptic future  sorta had a good idea but didn't turn  out to be great in my opinion  hopefully tribes of europa will have  something more impressive inside their  cube  and by this time next year we'll all be  anticipating the next season  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already  after i see the rest of the season i may  come back and do an ending explain video  so check back for that and thanks for  watching i'll talk to you soon
 

